that the price is already the lowest

281
00:10:39,191 --> 00:10:41,638
possible, or that the online quote was

282
00:10:41,638 --> 00:10:42,281
a mistake.

283
00:10:42,461 --> 00:10:45,277
Stay calm and return to the out-the-door

284
00:10:45,277 --> 00:10:45,770
number.

285
00:10:45,950 --> 00:10:47,502
Ask what they can do on the

286
00:10:47,502 --> 00:10:48,191
total price.

287
00:10:48,371 --> 00:10:50,014
You do not need to explain why

288
00:10:50,014 --> 00:10:51,274
you want a better deal.

289
00:10:51,454 --> 00:10:54,112
The competing quote explains it for you.

290
00:10:54,463 --> 00:10:55,786
Here is the twist.

291
00:10:55,966 --> 00:10:57,475
Use your written quotes.

292
00:10:57,655 --> 00:10:59,956
Show the dealer the best out-the-door offer

293
00:10:59,956 --> 00:11:01,453
you have and ask if they can

294
00:11:01,453 --> 00:11:01,881
beat it.

295
00:11:02,061 --> 00:11:03,838
Be polite and specific.

296
00:11:04,018 --> 00:11:06,489
A real competing offer is much more

297
00:11:06,489 --> 00:11:09,312
powerful than saying you think the price

298
00:11:09,312 --> 00:11:10,159
is too high.

299
00:11:10,339 --> 00:11:11,885
And if they cannot beat it,

300
00:11:11,885 --> 00:11:13,602
you already know where to buy.

301
00:11:13,952 --> 00:11:16,947
Step six: handle the trade-in separately.

302
00:11:17,127 --> 00:11:18,311
Before you visit,

303
00:11:18,311 --> 00:11:20,958
get offers for your current truck from

304
00:11:20,958 --> 00:11:23,118
other dealers or online buyers.

305
00:11:23,298 --> 00:11:25,339
Only bring up the trade after the

306
00:11:25,339 --> 00:11:27,628
new truck price is agreed in writing.

307
00:11:27,808 --> 00:11:30,125
That way, the dealer cannot give you

308
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:32,056
a big discount on one side and

309
00:11:32,056 --> 00:11:33,729
take it back on the other.

310
00:11:34,079 --> 00:11:35,368
Here is the twist.

311
00:11:35,548 --> 00:11:36,632
In many states,

312
00:11:36,632 --> 00:11:39,232
trading in at the dealer reduces the

313
00:11:39,232 --> 00:11:40,532
sales tax you pay,

314
00:11:40,532 --> 00:11:42,988
because tax is charged only on the

315
00:11:42,988 --> 00:11:45,877
difference between the new truck and the

316
00:11:45,877 --> 00:11:46,311
trade.

317
00:11:46,491 --> 00:11:48,820
That can make a slightly lower trade

318
00:11:48,820 --> 00:11:51,149
offer from the dealer worth the same

319
00:11:51,149 --> 00:11:53,219
as a higher offer from a private

320
00:11:53,219 --> 00:11:53,608
buyer.

321
00:11:53,788 --> 00:11:56,513
Check your state's rules and compare the

322
00:11:56,513 --> 00:11:57,398
real numbers.

323
00:11:57,748 --> 00:12:00,396
And be honest about your trade's condition.

324
00:12:00,576 --> 00:12:03,602
Clean it, gather the service records,

325
00:12:03,602 --> 00:12:04,747
and fix small,

326
00:12:04,747 --> 00:12:07,774
cheap problems before you get offers.

327
00:12:07,954 --> 00:12:10,081
A truck that looks cared for gets

328
00:12:10,081 --> 00:12:10,984
better offers.

329
00:12:11,164 --> 00:12:13,094
But do not spend big money on

330
00:12:13,094 --> 00:12:15,025
repairs right before selling,

331
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:17,554
because you rarely get that money back

332
00:12:17,554 --> 00:12:19,152
in a higher trade value.

333
00:12:19,501 --> 00:12:22,706
Step seven: survive the finance office.

334
00:12:22,886 --> 00:12:24,709
After you agree on the price,

335
00:12:24,709 --> 00:12:26,783
you will go to the finance office

336
00:12:26,783 --> 00:12:27,286
to sign.

337
00:12:27,466 --> 00:12:29,806
This is where extended warranties,

338
00:12:29,806 --> 00:12:33,108
protection plans and other products are offered.

339
00:12:33,288 --> 00:12:34,820
According to CarEdge,

340
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:38,320
protection plans on quotes averaged one thousand

341
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:40,726
four hundred ninety-four dollars,

342
00:12:40,726 --> 00:12:44,736
and theft protection averaged seven hundred eighty-two.

343
00:12:45,085 --> 00:12:46,432
Here is the twist.

344
00:12:46,612 --> 00:12:49,313
Products sold in the finance office are

345
00:12:49,313 --> 00:12:52,083
often negotiable, and many can be bought

346
00:12:52,083 --> 00:12:52,499
later.

347
00:12:52,679 --> 00:12:55,306
Decide before you arrive what you want,

348
00:12:55,306 --> 00:12:56,115
if anything.

349
00:12:56,295 --> 00:12:58,487
Ask for the price of each item

350
00:12:58,487 --> 00:12:59,290
separately.

351
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:02,170
And check the final contract carefully:

352
00:13:02,170 --> 00:13:04,177
the price, the interest rate,

353
00:13:04,177 --> 00:13:06,600
the loan length and every line item

354
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:08,607
should match what you agreed.

355
00:13:08,787 --> 00:13:10,599
Do not sign until they do.

356
00:13:10,948 --> 00:13:12,899
One more finance office tip.

357
00:13:13,079 --> 00:13:15,003
Ask for the interest rate as a

358
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:16,864
number, not just the payment.

359
00:13:17,044 --> 00:13:19,011
If the rate is higher than your

360
00:13:19,011 --> 00:13:21,358
pre-approval, ask them to match it or

361
00:13:21,358 --> 00:13:22,500
use your own loan.

362
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:25,371
Dealers can legally offer a rate above

363
00:13:25,371 --> 00:13:28,062
the lender's approval and keep part of

364
00:13:28,062 --> 00:13:29,124
the difference.

365
00:13:29,304 --> 00:13:32,054
Knowing your number stops that from happening

366
00:13:32,054 --> 00:13:32,543
quietly.

367
00:13:32,893 --> 00:13:35,332
Step eight: be ready to walk away.

368
00:13:35,512 --> 00:13:37,576
This is the step that makes every

369
00:13:37,576 --> 00:13:38,577
other step work.

370
00:13:38,757 --> 00:13:40,720
If the numbers are not right,

371
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:42,209
thank the salesperson,

372
00:13:42,209 --> 00:13:44,308
leave your contact information,

373
00:13:44,308 --> 00:13:44,782
and go.

374
00:13:44,962 --> 00:13:46,408
You have other quotes,

375
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:48,840
your own financing and a clear target

376
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,235
price.

377
00:13:49,415 --> 00:13:51,492
The dealer knows that a buyer who

378
00:13:51,492 --> 00:13:53,443
walks away might not come back.

379
00:13:53,793 --> 00:13:55,210
Here is the twist.

380
00:13:55,390 --> 00:13:58,127
Many buyers find the best offer comes

381
00:13:58,127 --> 00:13:59,385
after they leave,

382
00:13:59,385 --> 00:14:01,382
in a phone call or an email

383
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,344
the next day.

384
00:14:02,524 --> 00:14:04,800
Walking away is not a failure.

385
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,895
It is a negotiation tool.

386
00:14:07,075 --> 00:14:09,631
The only buyer who cannot walk away

387
00:14:09,631 --> 00:14:11,968
is one who has already fallen in

388
00:14:11,968 --> 00:14:14,086
love with a single truck on a

389
00:14:14,086 --> 00:14:14,889
single lot.

390
00:14:15,238 --> 00:14:17,775
And walk away early if something feels

391
00:14:17,775 --> 00:14:18,176
wrong.

392
00:14:18,356 --> 00:14:20,842
If the price changes between the quote

393
00:14:20,842 --> 00:14:21,758
and the visit,

394
00:14:21,758 --> 00:14:24,506
if add-ons appear that were not mentioned,

395
00:14:24,506 --> 00:14:26,600
or if the dealer refuses to show

396
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,629
an itemized out-the-door price,

397
00:14:28,629 --> 00:14:30,853
those are signs that the deal will

398
00:14:30,853 --> 00:14:31,835
not get better.

399
00:14:32,015 --> 00:14:34,256
There are many trucks and many dealers.

400
00:14:34,436 --> 00:14:35,840
You can always find another.

401
00:14:36,190 --> 00:14:38,591
Now a special warning about lease ads,

402
00:14:38,591 --> 00:14:40,675
because they are some of the most

403
00:14:40,675 --> 00:14:43,075
confusing numbers in the truck market.

404
00:14:43,255 --> 00:14:47,110
According to CarEdge's October twenty twenty-six list,

405
00:14:47,110 --> 00:14:51,036
a twenty twenty-six Chevrolet Silverado fifteen hundred

406
00:14:51,036 --> 00:14:54,533
lease was advertised at three hundred twenty-nine

407
00:14:54,533 --> 00:14:57,317
dollars a month for twenty-four months,

408
00:14:57,317 --> 00:15:00,958
with nine thousand six hundred eighty-eight dollars

409
00:15:00,958 --> 00:15:02,029
due at signing.

410
00:15:02,378 --> 00:15:04,573
Here is how to see the real

411
00:15:04,573 --> 00:15:04,979
cost.

412
00:15:05,159 --> 00:15:08,480
Spread the due-at-signing amount across the months.

413
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:11,756
Nine thousand six hundred eighty-eight dollars over

414
00:15:11,756 --> 00:15:14,792
twenty-four months adds about four hundred dollars

415
00:15:14,792 --> 00:15:15,277
a month.

416
00:15:15,457 --> 00:15:17,418
So the real cost is closer to

417
00:15:17,418 --> 00:15:19,919
seven hundred thirty dollars a month,

418
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,947
not three hundred twenty-nine.

419
00:15:22,127 --> 00:15:24,938
Compare that with a twenty twenty-six Ram

420
00:15:24,938 --> 00:15:28,022
fifteen hundred lease listed at three hundred

421
00:15:28,022 --> 00:15:30,970
twenty-five dollars a month with only three

422
00:15:30,970 --> 00:15:33,369
hundred twenty-five due at signing,

423
00:15:33,369 --> 00:15:35,014
for twenty-seven months.

424
00:15:35,364 --> 00:15:37,774
Two ads with almost the same monthly

425
00:15:37,774 --> 00:15:40,183
payment can be very different deals.

426
00:15:40,363 --> 00:15:42,625
Always add the due-at-signing amount,

427
00:15:42,625 --> 00:15:44,704
divide it by the number of months,

428
00:15:44,704 --> 00:15:46,783
and add it to the monthly payment.

429
00:15:46,963 --> 00:15:49,675
That simple math reveals which lease is

430
00:15:49,675 --> 00:15:52,457
really cheaper, and it takes ten seconds

431
00:15:52,457 --> 00:15:54,126
with a phone calculator.

432
00:15:54,476 --> 00:15:57,359
Lease ads also hide other details in

433
00:15:57,359 --> 00:15:58,560
the fine print:

434
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:00,561
the annual mileage limit,

435
00:16:00,561 --> 00:16:02,162
the fees at the end,

436
00:16:02,162 --> 00:16:06,005
and whether the offer requires excellent credit.

437
00:16:06,185 --> 00:16:08,688
A Ford Maverick lease listed by CarEdge

438
00:16:08,688 --> 00:16:11,511
at three hundred ninety-nine dollars a month

439
00:16:11,511 --> 00:16:12,987
for forty-eight months,

440
00:16:12,987 --> 00:16:16,131
with one thousand three hundred ninety-eight due,

441
00:16:16,131 --> 00:16:19,018
looks very different from a twenty-four month

442
00:16:19,018 --> 00:16:19,339
deal.

443
00:16:19,519 --> 00:16:21,723
Always compare lease length,

444
00:16:21,723 --> 00:16:23,532
mileage and total cost,

445
00:16:23,532 --> 00:16:25,185
not just the payment.

446
00:16:25,534 --> 00:16:27,746
Here is one more tactic for hot

447
00:16:27,746 --> 00:16:29,459
trucks: get on the list.

448
00:16:29,639 --> 00:16:31,101
For high-demand models,

449
00:16:31,101 --> 00:16:33,264
some dealers keep a list of buyers

450
00:16:33,264 --> 00:16:35,490
who want to order at sticker price.

451
00:16:35,670 --> 00:16:38,056
Ask several dealers if they sell at

452
00:16:38,056 --> 00:16:40,852
sticker, put down a refundable deposit if

453
00:16:40,852 --> 00:16:42,079
they do, and wait.

454
00:16:42,259 --> 00:16:44,881
Patience can save the thousands of dollars

455
00:16:44,881 --> 00:16:47,191
that a market adjustment would add on

456
00:16:47,191 --> 00:16:48,876
a truck already on the lot.

457
00:16:49,226 --> 00:16:52,175
And consider dealers outside your area.

458
00:16:52,355 --> 00:16:54,987
A dealer two hours away might have

459
00:16:54,987 --> 00:16:58,625
more inventory, lower fees or bigger discounts.

460
00:16:58,805 --> 00:17:01,512
Driving a few hours to save thousands

461
00:17:01,512 --> 00:17:03,635
of dollars is often worth it.

462
00:17:03,815 --> 00:17:06,514
Just remember that warranty service can be

463
00:17:06,514 --> 00:17:08,442
done at any authorized dealer,

464
00:17:08,442 --> 00:17:10,499
so buying far away does not mean

465
00:17:10,499 --> 00:17:12,685
you must return there for repairs.

466
00:17:13,034 --> 00:17:15,277
Finally, keep emotion out of it as

467
00:17:15,277 --> 00:17:16,332
long as you can.

468
00:17:16,512 --> 00:17:17,875
Test drive the truck,

469
00:17:17,875 --> 00:17:20,081
but do not tell the salesperson it

470
00:17:20,081 --> 00:17:21,899
is the one you have to have.

471
00:17:22,079 --> 00:17:24,523
A buyer who sounds ready to buy

472
00:17:24,523 --> 00:17:27,361
at any price gets offered any price.

473
00:17:27,541 --> 00:17:29,757
A buyer who sounds like they are

474
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,942
comparing several trucks gets offered the best

475
00:17:32,942 --> 00:17:33,358
price.

476
00:17:33,707 --> 00:17:36,262
So what is the pattern behind all

477
00:17:36,262 --> 00:17:37,190
eight steps?

478
00:17:37,370 --> 00:17:39,077
Control the information.

479
00:17:39,257 --> 00:17:41,463
The dealer negotiates every day.

480
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:44,162
You negotiate a truck every few years.

481
00:17:44,342 --> 00:17:46,978
The steps in this video close that

482
00:17:46,978 --> 00:17:49,381
gap: you know the market price,

483
00:17:49,381 --> 00:17:51,785
the incentives, your financing,

484
00:17:51,785 --> 00:17:53,102
your trade value,

485
00:17:53,102 --> 00:17:56,203
and your walk-away number before you sit

486
00:17:56,203 --> 00:17:56,591
down.

487
00:17:56,941 --> 00:17:58,891
And here is the final twist.

488
00:17:59,071 --> 00:18:01,893
Negotiating is not about being aggressive.

489
00:18:02,073 --> 00:18:04,260
The best negotiators are calm,

490
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:05,718
polite and prepared.

491
00:18:05,898 --> 00:18:07,415
They ask clear questions,

492
00:18:07,415 --> 00:18:08,931
they compare real offers,

493
00:18:08,931 --> 00:18:10,751
and they are willing to leave.

494
00:18:10,931 --> 00:18:12,523
In twenty twenty-six,

495
00:18:12,523 --> 00:18:15,253
with record payments and long loans,

496
00:18:15,253 --> 00:18:18,361
that preparation is worth more than ever.

497
00:18:18,712 --> 00:18:20,481
And do not forget the extras that

498
00:18:20,481 --> 00:18:21,928
should come with the truck.

499
00:18:22,108 --> 00:18:23,397
Ask for two keys,

500
00:18:23,397 --> 00:18:24,838
all the floor mats,

501
00:18:24,838 --> 00:18:28,175
the owner's manual and any accessories shown

502
00:18:28,175 --> 00:18:29,236
in the photos.

503
00:18:29,416 --> 00:18:32,061
Make sure any promised repair or item

504
00:18:32,061 --> 00:18:33,991
is written on the contract.

505
00:18:34,171 --> 00:18:36,957
These small items cost money to replace,

506
00:18:36,957 --> 00:18:39,325
and they are easiest to get before

507
00:18:39,325 --> 00:18:39,952
you sign.

508
00:18:40,303 --> 00:18:43,310
Finally, inspect the truck before you sign.

509
00:18:43,490 --> 00:18:45,532
Walk around it in good light,

510
00:18:45,532 --> 00:18:47,574
check for scratches or dents,

511
00:18:47,574 --> 00:18:50,038
and make sure the options match the

512
00:18:50,038 --> 00:18:51,094
window sticker.

513
00:18:51,274 --> 00:18:52,514
Once you drive away,

514
00:18:52,514 --> 00:18:54,559
it becomes much harder to prove a

515
00:18:54,559 --> 00:18:56,603
problem came from the dealer lot.

516
00:18:56,953 --> 00:18:59,691
A quick example shows how the steps

517
00:18:59,691 --> 00:19:00,239
add up.

518
00:19:00,419 --> 00:19:03,331
Imagine a buyer who saves three percent

519
00:19:03,331 --> 00:19:04,825
by comparing quotes,

520
00:19:04,825 --> 00:19:08,036
avoids one thousand four hundred dollars in

521
00:19:08,036 --> 00:19:11,771
add-ons, skips a fifteen hundred dollar protection

522
00:19:11,771 --> 00:19:13,489
plan they did not need,

523
00:19:13,489 --> 00:19:16,252
and uses a zero percent offer instead

524
00:19:16,252 --> 00:19:17,671
of an average rate.

525
00:19:17,851 --> 00:19:19,962
On a sixty thousand dollar truck,

526
00:19:19,962 --> 00:19:22,072
that can add up to many thousands

527
00:19:22,072 --> 00:19:24,759
of dollars, without any yelling or tricks.

528
00:19:25,109 --> 00:19:28,013
And none of these steps require special

529
00:19:28,013 --> 00:19:28,534
skills.

530
00:19:28,714 --> 00:19:30,112
They require time:

531
00:19:30,112 --> 00:19:31,898
an evening of research,

532
00:19:31,898 --> 00:19:32,908
a few emails,

533
00:19:32,908 --> 00:19:34,461
a call to your bank.

534
00:19:34,641 --> 00:19:37,247
That time can easily be worth more

535
00:19:37,247 --> 00:19:39,471
per hour than almost any job.

536
00:19:39,651 --> 00:19:41,845
Treat buying a truck like the major

537
00:19:41,845 --> 00:19:43,412
financial decision it is,

538
00:19:43,412 --> 00:19:45,544
and the dealer will treat you like

539
00:19:45,544 --> 00:19:46,547
a serious buyer.

540
00:19:46,897 --> 00:19:49,789
So here is the eight-step checklist one

541
00:19:49,789 --> 00:19:50,531
more time.

542
00:19:50,711 --> 00:19:51,965
Know what people pay.

543
00:19:52,145 --> 00:19:53,352
Pick the right time.

544
00:19:53,532 --> 00:19:55,018
Get pre-approved.

545
00:19:55,198 --> 00:19:57,601
Get three written out-the-door quotes.

546
00:19:57,781 --> 00:20:00,034
Negotiate only the price.

547
00:20:00,214 --> 00:20:02,025
Handle the trade-in separately.

548
00:20:02,205 --> 00:20:04,968
Check every line in the finance office.

549
00:20:05,148 --> 00:20:06,774
And be ready to walk away.

550
00:20:07,124 --> 00:20:08,682
We put the full version,

551
00:20:08,682 --> 00:20:10,761
with scripts for what to say and

552
00:20:10,761 --> 00:20:12,254
the numbers to compare,

553
00:20:12,254 --> 00:20:15,437
into the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

554
00:20:15,617 --> 00:20:17,872
The link is in the description and

555
00:20:17,872 --> 00:20:19,332
in the pinned comment.

556
00:20:19,512 --> 00:20:21,883
Subscribe for the next video,

557
00:20:21,883 --> 00:20:25,154
about why truck insurance costs so much.

558
00:20:25,334 --> 00:20:27,246
And tell us in the comments:

559
00:20:27,246 --> 00:20:29,364
what is the best truck deal you

560
00:20:29,364 --> 00:20:29,978
ever got?

561
00:20:30,158 --> 00:20:31,342
Thanks for watching.
